WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.514 --> 00:00:01.547
- Good morning, Believe Nation!

00:00:01.547 --> 00:00:05.333
Today's message is follow your own dreams.

00:00:05.333 --> 00:00:07.358
Over to you PewDiePie.

00:00:07.358 --> 00:00:09.331
(rooster crowing)

00:00:09.331 --> 00:00:11.893
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.893 --> 00:00:14.368
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:14.368 --> 00:00:17.785
♫ I wake up ever morning

00:00:18.813 --> 00:00:21.563
- Follow your own goddamn dreams.

00:00:23.117 --> 00:00:24.923
Not what your mom wants you to do,

00:00:24.923 --> 00:00:27.147
not what your dad wants you to do,

00:00:27.147 --> 00:00:30.003
not what you think you should be doing,

00:00:30.003 --> 00:00:34.480
but doing what you want
to do more than anything.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:37.480
It's been said so many times before,

00:00:38.504 --> 00:00:41.686
but really, if you don't make
your own decisions in life,

00:00:41.686 --> 00:00:43.577
someone else is going
to make them for you,

00:00:43.577 --> 00:00:46.354
and by the end of it, you won't be happy.

00:00:46.354 --> 00:00:50.047
So you might as well do
what it is you want to do.

00:00:50.047 --> 00:00:51.860
- So I think somewhere along the lines,

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:54.319
in everyone's life, you
have to make the decision

00:00:54.319 --> 00:00:58.534
at some point, whether you
are living your version

00:00:58.534 --> 00:01:02.229
of your life, or someone
else's version of your life.

00:01:02.229 --> 00:01:05.963
Because along the way,
people are always going

00:01:05.963 --> 00:01:09.355
to have opinions on what
you should and shouldn't do.

00:01:09.355 --> 00:01:11.435
They're going to have opinions
on what career you should take,

00:01:11.435 --> 00:01:13.249
have opinions on what
school you should go to,

00:01:13.249 --> 00:01:15.911
have opinions on whether to
start that business or not,

00:01:15.911 --> 00:01:17.279
to move to that country or not,

00:01:17.279 --> 00:01:20.141
have opinions on what color
socks you're going to wear today.

00:01:20.141 --> 00:01:22.882
People will have opinions on everything.

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:24.321
And if all you do is live your life

00:01:24.321 --> 00:01:27.258
according to other people's
opinions and expectations,

00:01:27.258 --> 00:01:30.119
you are never going to
get to the point where

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:32.555
one, you're happy, and two,
you're actually doing the thing

00:01:32.555 --> 00:01:34.762
that you can be great at.

00:01:34.762 --> 00:01:36.215
It's not going to happen.

00:01:36.215 --> 00:01:38.046
Now, in the early days
of being a human being,

00:01:38.046 --> 00:01:39.945
you listen to your parents, right?

00:01:39.945 --> 00:01:42.159
You go to the classes and
schools that they send you to

00:01:42.159 --> 00:01:44.443
and you listen to them, and
hopefully you're a little bit

00:01:44.443 --> 00:01:45.915
respectful, as well.

00:01:45.915 --> 00:01:48.619
But as you get older, at some point,

00:01:48.619 --> 00:01:51.339
you need to realize that
you're an adult human being.

00:01:51.339 --> 00:01:54.780
And you need to make decisions
and take accountability

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:57.394
for your life, as well.

00:01:57.394 --> 00:01:59.109
If you're not where you want to be,

00:01:59.109 --> 00:02:01.173
if you're in the wrong major,

00:02:01.173 --> 00:02:02.685
if you're taking the wrong classes,

00:02:02.685 --> 00:02:04.005
if you're in the wrong
business or wrong career,

00:02:04.005 --> 00:02:07.872
it's not your parents' fault,
it's not your friends' fault,

00:02:07.872 --> 00:02:09.896
it's not your advisor's fault.

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:11.535
It's your own fault.

00:02:11.535 --> 00:02:13.329
You, that's it, it's your fault.

00:02:13.329 --> 00:02:15.621
You are where you are
because of you, period.

00:02:15.621 --> 00:02:18.982
You can't blame other
people for your decisions

00:02:18.982 --> 00:02:20.363
for the rest of your life.

00:02:20.363 --> 00:02:21.889
So if you want to break free,

00:02:21.889 --> 00:02:23.679
you have to take that responsibility

00:02:23.679 --> 00:02:25.504
and start doing something about it.

00:02:25.504 --> 00:02:27.211
I find that you're going
to have two kinds of people

00:02:27.211 --> 00:02:29.037
who will be the haters in your life.

00:02:29.037 --> 00:02:31.378
The people who will
give you the bad advice,

00:02:31.378 --> 00:02:33.771
the wrong advice, the unsupportive advice.

00:02:33.771 --> 00:02:35.517
The first group is going to be the people

00:02:35.517 --> 00:02:37.141
who are jealous of you.

00:02:37.141 --> 00:02:39.009
The people who are just nasty people,

00:02:39.009 --> 00:02:41.939
haters of the little man, and
they tell you all the reasons

00:02:41.939 --> 00:02:44.010
why you can't do the
thing that you want to do.

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.486
You want to go and start that business,

00:02:45.486 --> 00:02:47.733
they tell you how you
don't have the education,

00:02:47.733 --> 00:02:49.601
the connections, and the
money, and the resources,

00:02:49.601 --> 00:02:51.075
and you've never done them before,

00:02:51.075 --> 00:02:52.338
and who are you to think
you can go out and do that.

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:54.397
No one from this town has ever gone on

00:02:54.397 --> 00:02:56.056
and done something that big.

00:02:56.056 --> 00:02:57.446
All of those people.

00:02:57.446 --> 00:03:00.578
And often, if you look at their life,

00:03:00.578 --> 00:03:02.486
it's really just based out of fear,

00:03:02.486 --> 00:03:04.388
insecurity, and jealousy.

00:03:04.388 --> 00:03:05.976
Maybe at one point, they took a big shot,

00:03:05.976 --> 00:03:07.672
they tried to follow their dream,

00:03:07.672 --> 00:03:09.096
they tried to do something important,

00:03:09.096 --> 00:03:10.235
and it didn't work out.

00:03:10.235 --> 00:03:12.746
And because they didn't have success,

00:03:12.746 --> 00:03:15.518
now nobody around them can have success.

00:03:15.518 --> 00:03:17.943
Now every idea or everybody
who tries to do something

00:03:17.943 --> 00:03:19.746
on their own, that's a bad idea,

00:03:19.746 --> 00:03:23.371
and they need to be the anchor
for everybody around them.

00:03:23.371 --> 00:03:24.620
Right?

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:29.581
You're trying to rise up, and
they want to pull you back down.

00:03:29.581 --> 00:03:32.033
They're going to be
that anchor around you.

00:03:32.033 --> 00:03:35.396
And those are the easier
people, actually, to ignore.

00:03:35.396 --> 00:03:37.735
Their words may sting,
they may be more visceral

00:03:37.735 --> 00:03:39.105
and more angry with you,

00:03:39.105 --> 00:03:41.262
but recognizing that they
haven't done the thing

00:03:41.262 --> 00:03:44.127
that you want to do makes it easier.

00:03:44.127 --> 00:03:47.171
It's now the second
group who are the people

00:03:47.171 --> 00:03:48.741
who are doing it out of love.

00:03:48.741 --> 00:03:51.583
They're not doing it out
of fear and jealousy,

00:03:51.583 --> 00:03:53.057
they're doing it out of love.

00:03:53.057 --> 00:03:54.893
You know, your parents may tell you

00:03:54.893 --> 00:03:56.456
not to go out and start that business,

00:03:56.456 --> 00:03:58.177
not to go out and chase
that dream of yours.

00:03:58.177 --> 00:04:00.695
Your closest friends may
tell you that's really risky.

00:04:00.695 --> 00:04:02.227
Don't go out and do that.

00:04:02.227 --> 00:04:04.041
And they're doing it out of love,

00:04:04.041 --> 00:04:05.417
because they care about you.

00:04:05.417 --> 00:04:06.903
It's not that they're
jealous or they hate you.

00:04:06.903 --> 00:04:08.157
They love you.

00:04:08.157 --> 00:04:11.074
The challenge is, they see success,

00:04:12.654 --> 00:04:15.630
success through their eyes,

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:19.129
through their narrow, limited view, right?

00:04:19.129 --> 00:04:23.410
And success may be go out
and get a safe, secure job.

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:26.043
Go out and be a doctor, be an
accountant, or be a lawyer.

00:04:26.043 --> 00:04:27.140
Go out and do this safe thing.

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:29.558
Or, do what I did, right?

00:04:29.558 --> 00:04:32.793
I went and I did this and I had success,

00:04:32.793 --> 00:04:34.180
so you should follow in my footsteps,

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:36.281
because that's what success looks like.

00:04:36.281 --> 00:04:38.039
And the way to break
through is understanding

00:04:38.039 --> 00:04:41.571
that your version of success
does not look like theirs.

00:04:41.571 --> 00:04:43.150
And what really helps is to think about,

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:45.625
these people that are giving me advice,

00:04:45.625 --> 00:04:47.809
my parents, the people
around me, the haters,

00:04:47.809 --> 00:04:50.216
these people that are
throwing opinions on me,

00:04:50.216 --> 00:04:52.046
who are telling me all these
things that I should be doing

00:04:52.046 --> 00:04:56.840
that I'm not, have they
done what you want to do?

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:00.043
Have they gone where you want to go?

00:05:00.043 --> 00:05:02.141
And if the answer is no, then who are they

00:05:02.141 --> 00:05:03.664
to give you advice?

00:05:03.664 --> 00:05:05.424
How can they tell you what to do

00:05:05.424 --> 00:05:08.980
if they've never done what you want to do?

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:11.411
If anything, you want to take
the opposite of their advice.

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:14.850
I don't want your life, and
so I'm going to go this way

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:17.243
and do the opposite of
what you're telling me.

00:05:17.243 --> 00:05:19.620
Now, you don't have to be mean
and rude and in their face

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:21.245
about it, especially if
it's coming from a place

00:05:21.245 --> 00:05:22.600
of love from them.

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:24.890
But in your head, that's
what you're thinking.

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:27.910
These people have not done
what I'm trying to do.

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:29.025
They don't know how to give me the advice

00:05:29.025 --> 00:05:30.175
to help me get there.

00:05:30.175 --> 00:05:31.603
I need to find different mentors,

00:05:31.603 --> 00:05:34.243
different guides, a different path,

00:05:34.243 --> 00:05:35.940
that is different from
what they're telling me.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:38.888
And if you shrink down
and you don't accept that

00:05:38.888 --> 00:05:41.215
and you say, "You know
what, you guys are right,"

00:05:41.215 --> 00:05:43.802
because you're afraid to stand up to them,

00:05:43.802 --> 00:05:47.715
then you're never ever
ever ever going to reach

00:05:47.715 --> 00:05:49.510
your potential, never.

00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:50.953
You're never going to be fully happy.

00:05:50.953 --> 00:05:52.981
You're always going to wonder what if.

00:05:52.981 --> 00:05:55.254
You're always going to think
that you could be doing more.

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:57.367
And the longer you stay on that path,

00:05:57.367 --> 00:06:00.191
the more boxed in and
boxed in and boxed in

00:06:00.191 --> 00:06:01.600
you're going to get.

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:04.353
And you've built a life for yourself

00:06:04.353 --> 00:06:06.628
where it's okay to shrink down.

00:06:06.628 --> 00:06:09.168
Where it's okay to play the smaller game

00:06:09.168 --> 00:06:11.901
and just live inside this box.

00:06:11.901 --> 00:06:15.917
Where every time you get
challenged by anybody,

00:06:15.917 --> 00:06:19.417
you've conditioned yourself to shrink down

00:06:21.081 --> 00:06:24.934
and just accept that
that's the way life is.

00:06:24.934 --> 00:06:28.198
And you're now going to
teach this to others.

00:06:28.198 --> 00:06:30.126
You're going to teach
this to your friends.

00:06:30.126 --> 00:06:31.683
You're going to teach this to your kids.

00:06:31.683 --> 00:06:35.583
You're going to teach playing
small and limited thinking

00:06:35.583 --> 00:06:38.819
onto the next generation, to your kids.

00:06:38.819 --> 00:06:42.596
And I want that cycle of
mediocrity to stop with you.

00:06:42.596 --> 00:06:44.744
I want you to practice being bold.

00:06:44.744 --> 00:06:47.391
I want you to practice
listening to yourself,

00:06:47.391 --> 00:06:49.031
understanding what you're all about

00:06:49.031 --> 00:06:49.930
and what your dreams are.

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:52.764
When you have an idea,
you start, you go for it,

00:06:52.764 --> 00:06:54.104
you push it forward.

00:06:54.104 --> 00:06:56.593
I want you to be a source of inspiration

00:06:56.593 --> 00:06:58.121
for the people around you.

00:06:58.121 --> 00:07:01.125
Where you don't need to yell
at them and show them off

00:07:01.125 --> 00:07:02.954
and tell them how they're wrong.

00:07:02.954 --> 00:07:05.438
You're just going to go
out and do your thing.

00:07:05.438 --> 00:07:06.935
And you may fail in the early days,

00:07:06.935 --> 00:07:08.486
but if you stick out and you persevere,

00:07:08.486 --> 00:07:09.489
you're going to have success.

00:07:09.489 --> 00:07:11.513
And that will be an inspiration

00:07:11.513 --> 00:07:12.858
to the people around you, saying,

00:07:12.858 --> 00:07:14.663
"Look what he's doing."

00:07:14.663 --> 00:07:17.068
"Look what she's doing, huh.

00:07:17.068 --> 00:07:19.235
"I can do something, too."

00:07:21.888 --> 00:07:23.778
That's what I want for you.

00:07:23.778 --> 00:07:25.614
And I hope you want it for yourself, too.

00:07:25.614 --> 00:07:26.447
Believe.

00:07:27.501 --> 00:07:29.297
So the question of the
day today is, I'm curious,

00:07:29.297 --> 00:07:33.464
what was the hardest part
about living your own dreams?

00:07:35.127 --> 00:07:37.469
What was the hardest part?

00:07:37.469 --> 00:07:38.743
Leave it in the comments below.

00:07:38.743 --> 00:07:40.068
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:07:40.068 --> 00:07:42.411
I also want to give a quick
shoutout to Reynaldo Espinoza

00:07:42.411 --> 00:07:44.751
from selfbuiltempire.com.

00:07:44.751 --> 00:07:46.645
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book

00:07:46.645 --> 00:07:49.833
Your One Word, it really,
really, really means a lot to me.

00:07:49.833 --> 00:07:51.350
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:07:51.350 --> 00:07:52.812
I believe in you.

00:07:52.812 --> 00:07:54.756
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself.

00:07:54.756 --> 00:07:56.773
And whatever your one word is,

00:07:56.773 --> 00:07:59.232
much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:07:59.232 --> 00:08:01.576
for another shot of an espresso.

00:08:01.576 --> 00:08:04.245
♫ I wake up every morning

00:08:04.245 --> 00:08:07.817
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:08:07.817 --> 00:08:09.840
Hey Believe Nation, we're
also look at doing a Top 10

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:12.116
on PewDiePie, and here is a sneak peek

00:08:12.116 --> 00:08:14.470
at some of the clips we're
thinking about using.

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:16.036
I hope you enjoy the bonus.

00:08:16.036 --> 00:08:20.547
- See how many spoons you
can balance on your face.

00:08:20.547 --> 00:08:22.288
What's the point of this?

00:08:22.288 --> 00:08:27.054
My job is so easy, I can
literally do what I feel like.

00:08:27.054 --> 00:08:29.866
It's kind of amazing, just
the fact that I can play

00:08:29.866 --> 00:08:31.632
video games for a living.

00:08:31.632 --> 00:08:33.798
And when I realized
that for the first time,

00:08:33.798 --> 00:08:35.145
like I was almost getting teary-eyed.

00:08:35.145 --> 00:08:36.885
Like it was my dream has come true.

00:08:36.885 --> 00:08:39.904
♫ All this time I've been finding myself

00:08:39.904 --> 00:08:43.840
♫ And I didn't know I was lost

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:46.123
I'd be happy not to be
number one. (laughs)

00:08:46.123 --> 00:08:48.701
I'm just a nerd who plays video games.

00:08:48.701 --> 00:08:51.532
I didn't seek the spotlight.

00:08:51.532 --> 00:08:53.007
Your parents will tell you you can be

00:08:53.007 --> 00:08:55.450
whatever you want to be
in life, which is true.

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:57.535
But what a lot of times
they don't tell you

00:08:57.535 --> 00:09:01.407
is that you have to work
really hard to get there.

00:09:01.407 --> 00:09:03.487
And another thing, maybe more importantly,

00:09:03.487 --> 00:09:05.474
is that you have to take risks.

00:09:05.474 --> 00:09:07.842
You have to venture into the unknown,

00:09:07.842 --> 00:09:10.440
and you might not know
what's going to happen,

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:11.479
and that's scary.

00:09:11.479 --> 00:09:15.058
But I think it's always
better to try than not try,

00:09:15.058 --> 00:09:16.367
no matter what.

00:09:16.367 --> 00:09:18.617
Except meth, not even once.

